--- !u!114 &1478462784
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1478462775}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 40fe67fde4a4351409089804b4848b92, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  _documentationText: 'YOLOv5 Object Detection Example

    Real-time COCO object
    detection using YOLOv5 with optional Unity Sentis or OpenCV DNN frameworks.

    

    Demonstrates:

    -
    Reading input frames via MultiSourceToMatHelper (webcam, video file, image file,
    or GPU readback)

    - Loading YOLOv5 ONNX/Sentis model and class names from
    StreamingAssets

    - Selecting OpenCV DNN vs Unity Sentis inference framework
    and async detection via MatSingleFlightSyncAsyncRunner

    - Converting RGBA
    frames to BGR, running YOLOv5ObjectDetectorMultiBackend, and visualizing output
    Mat

    

    OpenCV classes and APIs used:

    - Mat, Size, Scalar, Point

    -
    Imgproc: cvtColor

    - YOLOv5ObjectDetectorMultiBackend, MatSingleFlightSyncAsyncRunner,
    MultiBackendDnn

    - MultiSourceToMatHelper, OpenCVMatUnityUtils

    

    This
    example also works with YOLOv6 and YOLOv7 object-detection models that share
    the same

    input/output shapes as YOLOv5. Sample models and export notebooks:

    https://github.com/EnoxSoftware/YOLOv5WithOpenCVForUnityExample

    

    [Tested
    Models]

    yolov5n.onnx

    yolov6n.onnx

    yolov7-tiny.onnx'
  AlignmentSetting: 0
